=begin

  saga_hl_sagapanel.lic

  Saga-only floating workspace to improve Saga custom text highlights safely
  while the client is running. Reads prefs, never writes prefs live; always
  backs up, then writes an Import Settings JSON you load in Saga.

  Pair with saga-hl.lic if you want the short ;saga-hl start command.

  Safe flow:
    1. Read highlights from Saga prefs.json (no live prefs writes)
    2. Edit the in-memory working set (Browse / Diff / Backups / Tools)
    3. Snapshot under saga-hl-backups/<char>/
    4. Optionally run enabled improvers and/or Sync from another character
    5. Write saga-highlights.json (home directory)
    6. Saga -> Import Settings -> Custom highlights -> that file
    7. Undo via Backups mode (or *hl restore <backup-id>)

  In-game start:
    ;saga-hl                 - via saga-hl.lic launcher (optional)
    ;saga_hl_sagapanel       - this script directly

  Workspace (logged-in character only):
    Modes: Browse | Diff | Backups | Tools
    Close button / *hl close stops the workspace

  Commands:
    *hl help                 - This command list (story window)
    *hl status               - Counts / paths
    *hl close                - Close workspace and stop script
    *hl mode browse|diff|backups|tools
    *hl filter <text>        - Browse filter
    *hl page <n>             - Browse/diff/backup page
    *hl sel <id|idx>         - Select rule
    *hl del | *hl delmatch   - Delete selected / filtered
    *hl enable <id> 0|1      - Enable/disable rule
    *hl flag <name> 0|1      - Flag on selected
    *hl color <hex>          - Color on selected
    *hl pattern <text>       - Pattern on selected
    *hl group <name>         - Group on selected
    *hl diff | *hl diff backup <id>
    *hl diffshow all|added|removed|changed
    *hl discard              - Reload working from prefs
    *hl bak rename <id> <label...>
    *hl bak starter <id> | *hl bak load-starter
    *hl bak load <id> | *hl bak select <id>
    *hl set <improver> 0|1 | *hl toggle <name>
    *hl apply | *hl package | *hl backup | *hl write
    *hl syncsrc <from-key> | *hl syncgrp all|N 0|1 | *hl sync <from-key>
    *hl restore <backup-id>
    *hl char <name|instance> | *hl instance <id>   (CLI only)

  Improve+write vs Write only:
    Improve+write: backup, run every ON improver, then write the import file.
    Write only: write the current working set to the import file. No improvers.

  Implemented improver:
    Dedupe exact/color - exact pattern dupes, plus casefold-same patterns when
    RGB colors are close (distance <= 40).

  Not on this panel (optional Python CLI under Lich5/tools/saga-highlights):
    saga-hl import-hm-names / scan-names / filter-names

  Paths:
    Linux:   ~/.config/saga/prefs.json and saga-hl-backups/
    Windows: %APPDATA%\saga\prefs.json and saga-hl-backups\
    Starter: <saga-config>/saga-hl-starter/<char-slug>.json
    Import:  ~/saga-highlights.json  or  %USERPROFILE%\saga-highlights.json

  Story window:
    All echo lines are prefixed with [lich] for easy Saga filtering.
    Panel dialog XML (_respond) is not prefixed.

  Sharing / testing:
    Drop this file (and optionally saga-hl.lic) into Lich scripts/.
    Requires Saga + Lich >= 5.12.0. No Python CLI required for panel features.
    After Improve+write / Sync / Write only, use Saga Import Settings.

       creator: loraque (loraque@gmail.com)
        author: loraque (loraque@gmail.com)
          game: Gemstone
          tags: saga, frontend, panel, highlights, import, workspace
      required: Lich >= 5.12.0
       version: 0.5.0

  changelog:
    0.5.0 (2026-10-19)
      floating workspace redesign (resident=false): Browse / Diff / Backups /
        Tools modes; Close / *hl close exits cleanly
      Browse: filter/type/group/sort, paginated rows, detail flags/color/
        pattern/group, bulk enable/disable/delete match
      Diff: Ruby port of compare_sets vs live prefs or backup baseline
      Backups: paginated list, rename, starter set/load, load into working,
        compare vs working
      Tools: improvers + Improve+write / Write only / Backup / Sync
      editBox Enter wired via enterButton; list_backups accepts import-only snaps
    0.4.5 (2026-10-19)
      header cleanup for sharing: creator/author attribution, accurate feature
        list, paths, and test notes; remove stale Name-pack panel references
    0.4.4 (2026-10-19)
      remove Name pack from the panel (CLI/backend only)
    0.4.3 (2026-10-19)
      panel always uses the logged-in character (label only); remove top
        Character dropdown so Copy-from cannot steal the selection
      load_set_from_prefs no longer overwrites char_key (syncsrc bug)
    0.4.2 (2026-10-19)
      story echoes use [lich] prefix for easy Saga filter
      dedupe exact also collapses casefold-same patterns when colors are close
    0.4.1 (2026-10-19)
      fix Improve+write wiping a fresh Sync: use panel working set, not prefs
      Copy-from: multi-select group checkboxes (All/None)
    0.4.0 (2026-10-19)
      remove Instance tabs from panel (*hl instance remains CLI only)
      ASCII-clean panel and story text
      clarify Improve+write vs Write only
      Copy-from dropdown + Sync (skip existing patterns)
    0.3.0 (2026-10-18)
      redesign: character UI, rule counts, native widgets, restore picker,
        coach line; queue work on main loop
    0.2.1 (2026-10-18)
      fix *hl UpstreamHook match: strip FE <c> prefix; match like *exp/*ah
    0.2.0 (2026-10-18)
      fix dead panel clicks: queue *hl work on the script main loop
    0.1.0 (2026-10-18)
      initial panel: read prefs, backup, dedupe, write import JSON,
        Import Settings + restore prompts; Windows/Linux paths

  Maintainer note (outside game):
    Named regions use # BEGIN saga_hl/<name> / # END saga_hl/<name> markers.
    Prefer editing one region at a time; keep markers intact; bump version +
    changelog after changes.
      saga_hl/paths           OS paths, character key, starter dir
      saga_hl/model           highlight/group hashes, richness, clone, ids, merge
      saga_hl/io              prefs read, import JSON write, JSON helpers
      saga_hl/backup          versioned backups, rename, starter, restore
      saga_hl/compare         working vs live/backup diff
      saga_hl/improve_dedupe  exact + close-color dedupe
      saga_hl/editor          browse filter/sort/page/select/mutate
      saga_hl/pipeline        apply / package / sync
      saga_hl/messaging       story echoes, Import Settings copy, coach
      saga_hl/panel           dialog XML + mode layouts
      saga_hl/commands        *hl routing

=end

no_kill_all

require 'json'
require 'fileutils'
require 'time'

# BEGIN saga_hl/paths
module SagaHl
  extend self
  include Lich::Common if defined?(Lich::Common)

  DIALOG_ID = 'SagaHlPanel'
  ROW_HEIGHT = 18
  DROP_HEIGHT = 24
  BTN_HEIGHT = 22
  PANEL_WIDTH = 560
  BACKUP_KEEP = 40
  BROWSE_PAGE_SIZE = 18
  DIFF_PAGE_SIZE = 10
  RESTORE_PICK_LIMIT = 8
  BACKUP_PAGE_SIZE = 10
  IMPORT_BASENAME = 'saga-highlights.json'
  STARTER_DIRNAME = 'saga-hl-starter'

  INSTANCE_TITLES = {
    'prime' => 'Prime',
    'test' => 'Test',
    'platinum' => 'Platinum',
    'shattered' => 'Shattered',
    'prime-copy' => 'Prime copy'
  }.freeze

  # id, label, default_on, implemented
  IMPROVERS = [
    [:dedupe, 'Dedupe exact/color', true, true],
    [:gender, 'Gender pairs', false, false],
    [:spellprep, 'Enemy spell prep', false, false],
    [:palette, 'Palette colors', false, false],
    [:group_styles, 'Empath/Cleric groups', false, false]
  ].freeze

  STANDARD_PACKAGE = [:dedupe].freeze
  MODES = %w[browse diff backups tools].freeze

  # Max RGB Euclidean distance for "close" colors (#RRGGBB).
  COLOR_CLOSE_DIST = 40.0

  DEFAULT_COLORS = %w[
    #33ff08 #ffffff #00ffff #ff66ff #ff9000 #ffd700 #ffa500
    #c0c0ff #66ccff #ff6a6a #aaaaaa #32cd32 #ff6600 #ffad5f
  ].freeze

  FLAG_NAMES = %w[bold italic underline notify wholeWord caseSensitive regex].freeze

  COMPARE_FIELDS = %w[
    color scope wholeWord caseSensitive highlightType enabled
    regex bold italic underline notify sound
  ].freeze

  class << self
    attr_accessor :toggles, :last_backup_id, :last_import_path, :last_status,
                  :working, :dirty, :char_key, :pending_cmd, :instance_filter,
                  :last_action, :sync_source, :sync_group_sel, :sync_group_meta,
                  :_id_seq, :quit, :mode,
                  :browse_filter, :browse_type, :browse_group, :browse_sort,
                  :browse_page, :selected_id,
                  :diff_baseline, :diff_filter, :diff_page, :diff_cache,
                  :bak_page, :bak_selected, :bak_rename
  end

  # Synthetic ids for sync group filter
  SYNC_NONE = '__none__'.freeze
  SYNC_ORPHAN_PREFIX = '__orphan__:'.freeze
  NO_GROUP = '__nogroup__'.freeze

  def self.windows?
    ENV['OS'].to_s =~ /windows/i || File::ALT_SEPARATOR == '\\' ||
      RUBY_PLATFORM.to_s =~ /mswin|mingw|cygwin/i
  end

  def self.user_home
    if windows?
      ENV['USERPROFILE'].to_s.strip.empty? ? Dir.home : ENV['USERPROFILE']
    else
      Dir.home
    end
  end

  def self.saga_config_dir
    if windows?
      appdata = ENV['APPDATA'].to_s.strip
      base = appdata.empty? ? File.join(user_home, 'AppData', 'Roaming') : appdata
      File.join(base, 'saga')
    else
      File.join(user_home, '.config', 'saga')
    end
  end

  def self.prefs_path
    File.join(saga_config_dir, 'prefs.json')
  end

  def self.backup_root
    File.join(saga_config_dir, 'saga-hl-backups')
  end

  def self.logs_root
    File.join(saga_config_dir, 'logs')
  end

  def self.starter_root
    File.join(saga_config_dir, STARTER_DIRNAME)
  end

  def self.starter_pointer_path(key = nil)
    File.join(starter_root, "#{char_slug(key)}.json")
  end

  def self.starter_import_path(key = nil)
    File.join(starter_root, char_slug(key), 'import.json')
  end

  def self.import_path
    File.join(user_home, IMPORT_BASENAME)
  end

  def self.char_name
    if defined?(Char) && Char.respond_to?(:name) && !Char.name.to_s.strip.empty?
      Char.name.to_s.strip
    elsif defined?(XMLData) && XMLData.respond_to?(:name) && !XMLData.name.to_s.empty?
      XMLData.name.to_s.strip
    else
      'unknown'
    end
  end

  def self.normalize_char_key(raw)
    s = raw.to_s.strip.downcase
    return s if s.include?('|')
    "#{s}|prime"
  end

  def self.detect_char_key
    name = char_name.downcase
    prefs = read_prefs_hash
    keys = (prefs['characterSettings'] || {}).keys.map(&:to_s)
    matches = keys.select { |k| k.downcase.start_with?("#{name}|") }
    return matches.first if matches.size == 1
    return "#{name}|prime" if matches.any? { |k| k.downcase == "#{name}|prime" }
    return matches.first if matches.any?
    normalize_char_key(name)
  end

  def self.char_slug(key = nil)
    normalize_char_key(key || char_key || detect_char_key).tr('|', '-')
  end

  def self.split_char_key(key)
    name, inst = normalize_char_key(key).split('|', 2)
    [name.to_s, (inst.nil? || inst.empty?) ? 'prime' : inst]
  end

  def self.pretty_char_name(key)
    name, _inst = split_char_key(key)
    return name if name.empty?
    name[0].upcase + name[1..]
  end

  def self.pretty_instance(inst)
    INSTANCE_TITLES[inst.to_s.downcase] || inst.to_s.split(/[-_]/).map { |p| p[0].upcase + p[1..] }.join(' ')
  end

  def self.pretty_char_label(key, with_count: false)
    name, inst = split_char_key(key)
    base = "#{pretty_char_name(key)} (#{pretty_instance(inst)})"
    return base unless with_count
    "#{base} #{rule_count_for(key)}"
  end

  # Panel / story labels: keep ASCII (group names may contain em dashes).
  def self.ascii_label(text)
    text.to_s
        .gsub(/[—–]/, '-')
        .gsub(/[·•]/, ' ')
        .gsub(/[“”]/, '"')
        .gsub(/[‘’]/, "'")
        .gsub(/\s+/, ' ')
        .strip
  end

  # Working set is panel source of truth until character switch / reload.
  def self.working_for(key = nil)
    key = normalize_char_key(key || char_key || detect_char_key)
    if working && working['character'].to_s.downcase == key.downcase
      clone_set(working)
    else
      load_set_from_prefs(key)
    end
  end

  def self.ensure_working!
    self.char_key ||= detect_char_key
    unless working && working['character'].to_s.downcase == char_key.to_s.downcase
      self.working = load_set_from_prefs(char_key)
    end
    working
  end

  def self.list_character_keys
    (read_prefs_hash['characterSettings'] || {}).keys.map(&:to_s).sort_by(&:downcase)
  end

  def self.rule_count_for(key)
    prefs = read_prefs_hash
    cs = prefs['characterSettings'] || {}
    hit = cs.keys.find { |k| k.to_s.downcase == key.to_s.downcase }
    rec = hit ? cs[hit] : {}
    ((rec['customHighlights'] || []).size)
  end

  def self.group_count_for(key)
    prefs = read_prefs_hash
    cs = prefs['characterSettings'] || {}
    hit = cs.keys.find { |k| k.to_s.downcase == key.to_s.downcase }
    rec = hit ? cs[hit] : {}
    ((rec['highlightGroups'] || []).size)
  end

  def self.characters_by_instance
    list_character_keys.group_by { |k| split_char_key(k)[1] }
  end

  def self.instance_order
    known = INSTANCE_TITLES.keys
    present = characters_by_instance.keys
    (known & present) + (present - known).sort
  end

  def self.ensure_instance_filter!
    if instance_filter.to_s.empty?
      _n, inst = split_char_key(char_key || detect_char_key)
      self.instance_filter = inst
    end
    instance_filter
  end

  def self.ensure_ui_defaults!
    self.mode = 'browse' if mode.to_s.empty?
    self.browse_filter ||= ''
    self.browse_type ||= 'all'
    self.browse_group ||= 'all'
    self.browse_sort ||= 'pattern'
    self.browse_page = 0 if browse_page.nil?
    self.diff_baseline ||= 'live'
    self.diff_filter ||= 'all'
    self.diff_page = 0 if diff_page.nil?
    self.bak_page = 0 if bak_page.nil?
    self.bak_rename ||= ''
    self.quit = false if quit.nil?
  end
end
# END saga_hl/paths

# BEGIN saga_hl/model
module SagaHl
  def self.hl_richness(h)
    score = 0
    score += 1 if h['bold']
    score += 1 if h['italic']
    score += 1 if h['underline']
    score += 1 if h['notify']
    score += 1 if h['sound'].to_s.strip != ''
    score += 1 if h['regex']
    score += 1 if h['groupId'].to_s.strip != ''
    score
  end

  def self.new_id(prefix)
    self._id_seq = (_id_seq || 0) + 1
    "#{prefix}#{(Time.now.to_f * 1000).to_i}-#{_id_seq}"
  end

  def self.clone_set(set)
    {
      'character' => set['character'],
      'highlights' => (set['highlights'] || []).map { |h| h.dup },
      'groups' => (set['groups'] || []).map { |g| g.dup }
    }
  end

  def self.empty_set(character)
    { 'character' => character, 'highlights' => [], 'groups' => [] }
  end

  def self.group_name(set, group_id)
    return '' if group_id.to_s.empty?
    g = (set['groups'] || []).find { |x| x['id'] == group_id }
    g ? g['name'].to_s : group_id.to_s
  end

  def self.find_highlight(set, id)
    (set['highlights'] || []).find { |h| h['id'].to_s == id.to_s }
  end

  def self.find_group_by_name(set, name)
    want = name.to_s.downcase
    (set['groups'] || []).find { |g| g['name'].to_s.downcase == want }
  end

  def self.truthy_flag(h, name)
    v = h[name]
    return false if v.nil?
    return !!v if [true, false].include?(v)
    %w[1 true yes on].include?(v.to_s.downcase)
  end

  # Merge source into target by exact pattern. mode: skip | replace | clear
  def self.merge_sets!(target, source, mode: 'skip', copy_groups: true)
    mode = mode.to_s.downcase
    removed = 0
    if mode == 'clear'
      removed = (target['highlights'] || []).size
      target['highlights'] = []
    end

    target['groups'] ||= []
    target['highlights'] ||= []
    src_groups = {}
    (source['groups'] || []).each { |g| src_groups[g['id']] = g }
    tgt_by_name = {}
    target['groups'].each { |g| tgt_by_name[g['name'].to_s.downcase] = g }

    if copy_groups
      (source['groups'] || []).each do |g|
        key = g['name'].to_s.downcase
        next if key.empty? || tgt_by_name.key?(key)
        ng = g.dup
        ng['id'] = new_id('hlg1-')
        target['groups'] << ng
        tgt_by_name[key] = ng
      end
    end

    by_pattern = {}
    target['highlights'].each { |h| by_pattern[h['pattern'].to_s.downcase] = h }
    added = updated = skipped = 0

    (source['highlights'] || []).each do |h|
      pkey = h['pattern'].to_s.downcase
      group_id = nil
      if h['groupId'] && src_groups[h['groupId']]
        gname = src_groups[h['groupId']]['name'].to_s.downcase
        group_id = tgt_by_name[gname]['id'] if tgt_by_name[gname]
      end

      if by_pattern.key?(pkey)
        if mode == 'skip'
          skipped += 1
          next
        end
        if mode == 'replace'
          existing = by_pattern[pkey]
          %w[color scope wholeWord caseSensitive highlightType enabled bold italic underline notify sound regex].each do |f|
            existing[f] = h[f] if h.key?(f)
          end
          existing['groupId'] = group_id if group_id
          updated += 1
          next
        end
        skipped += 1
        next
      end

      new_h = h.dup
      new_h['id'] = new_id('hl1-')
      new_h['groupId'] = group_id
      target['highlights'] << new_h
      by_pattern[pkey] = new_h
      added += 1
    end

    { 'mode' => mode, 'added' => added, 'updated' => updated, 'removed' => removed, 'skipped' => skipped }
  end
end
# END saga_hl/model

# BEGIN saga_hl/io
module SagaHl
  def self.read_json_file(path)
    JSON.parse(File.read(path))
  end

  def self.write_json_file(path, data)
    FileUtils.mkdir_p(File.dirname(path))
    File.write(path, JSON.pretty_generate(data) + "\n")
  end

  def self.read_prefs_hash
    path = prefs_path
    return {} unless File.file?(path)
    read_json_file(path)
  rescue StandardError => e
    self.last_status = "prefs read failed: #{e.message}"
    {}
  end

  # Read a character's highlights from prefs. Does not change char_key / working.
  # Callers that switch the active character must set char_key themselves.
  def self.load_set_from_prefs(key = nil)
    key = normalize_char_key(key || char_key || detect_char_key)
    prefs = read_prefs_hash
    cs_all = prefs['characterSettings'] || {}
    cs = cs_all[key] || cs_all[key.downcase] || {}
    if cs.empty?
      hit = cs_all.keys.find { |k| k.to_s.downcase == key.downcase }
      cs = cs_all[hit] || {}
    end
    {
      'character' => key,
      'highlights' => (cs['customHighlights'] || []).map { |h| stringify_keys(h) },
      'groups' => (cs['highlightGroups'] || []).map { |g| stringify_keys(g) }
    }
  end

  def self.load_set_from_import_json(path, character = nil)
    data = read_json_file(path)
    cs = data['characterSettings'] || {}
    {
      'character' => (data['character'] || character || char_key),
      'highlights' => (cs['customHighlights'] || []).map { |h| stringify_keys(h) },
      'groups' => (cs['highlightGroups'] || []).map { |g| stringify_keys(g) }
    }
  end

  def self.stringify_keys(hash)
    out = {}
    (hash || {}).each { |k, v| out[k.to_s] = v }
    out
  end

  def self.to_saga_import(set)
    key = set['character']
    {
      'kind' => 'saga-settings',
      'version' => 1,
      'exportedAt' => Time.now.utc.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.000Z'),
      'character' => key,
      'categories' => ['highlights'],
      'characterSettings' => {
        'customHighlights' => set['highlights'],
        'highlightGroups' => set['groups']
      },
      'globals' => {}
    }
  end

  def self.write_import(set, path = nil)
    path ||= import_path
    write_json_file(path, to_saga_import(set))
    self.last_import_path = path
    path
  end
end
# END saga_hl/io

# BEGIN saga_hl/backup
module SagaHl
  def self.save_backup(set, reason: 'snapshot')
    stamp = Time.now.strftime('%Y%m%d-%H%M%S')
    safe = reason.to_s.gsub(/[^a-zA-Z0-9._-]+/, '-')[0, 48]
    safe = 'snapshot' if safe.empty?
    dir = File.join(backup_root, char_slug(set['character']), "#{stamp}_#{safe}")
    n = 2
    while File.exist?(dir)
      dir = File.join(backup_root, char_slug(set['character']), "#{stamp}_#{safe}-#{n}")
      n += 1
    end
    FileUtils.mkdir_p(dir)
    import_file = File.join(dir, 'import.json')
    write_json_file(import_file, to_saga_import(set))
    manifest = {
      'kind' => 'saga-hl-backup',
      'version' => 1,
      'character' => set['character'],
      'reason' => reason,
      'label' => reason,
      'createdAt' => Time.now.utc.iso8601,
      'highlightCount' => (set['highlights'] || []).size,
      'groupCount' => (set['groups'] || []).size
    }
    write_json_file(File.join(dir, 'manifest.json'), manifest)
    self.last_backup_id = File.basename(dir)
    last_backup_id
  end

  def self.list_backups(key = nil)
    root = File.join(backup_root, char_slug(key))
    return [] unless File.directory?(root)
    Dir.children(root).sort.reverse.filter_map do |name|
      imp = File.join(root, name, 'import.json')
      next unless File.file?(imp)
      man = File.join(root, name, 'manifest.json')
      begin
        m = File.file?(man) ? read_json_file(man) : {}
        {
          'id' => name,
          'reason' => m['reason'].to_s,
          'label' => (m['label'] || m['reason']).to_s,
          'highlightCount' => m['highlightCount'],
          'groupCount' => m['groupCount'],
          'createdAt' => m['createdAt'].to_s
        }
      rescue StandardError
        { 'id' => name, 'reason' => '', 'label' => '', 'highlightCount' => nil, 'groupCount' => nil, 'createdAt' => '' }
      end
    end
  end

  def self.backup_dir(backup_id, key = nil)
    File.join(backup_root, char_slug(key), backup_id)
  end

  def self.backup_import_path(backup_id, key = nil)
    File.join(backup_dir(backup_id, key), 'import.json')
  end

  def self.restore_backup_to_import(backup_id, key = nil)
    src = backup_import_path(backup_id, key)
    raise "backup not found: #{backup_id}" unless File.file?(src)
    data = read_json_file(src)
    path = write_import(
      {
        'character' => (data['character'] || key || char_key),
        'highlights' => (((data['characterSettings'] || {})['customHighlights']) || []),
        'groups' => (((data['characterSettings'] || {})['highlightGroups']) || [])
      }
    )
    path
  end

  def self.load_backup_set(backup_id, key = nil)
    src = backup_import_path(backup_id, key)
    raise "backup not found: #{backup_id}" unless File.file?(src)
    load_set_from_import_json(src, key || char_key)
  end

  # Rename directory keeping YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS_ prefix when present; update manifest.
  def self.rename_backup!(backup_id, new_label, key = nil)
    key = normalize_char_key(key || char_key || detect_char_key)
    old_dir = backup_dir(backup_id, key)
    raise "backup not found: #{backup_id}" unless File.directory?(old_dir)

    label = ascii_label(new_label).gsub(/[^a-zA-Z0-9._ -]+/, ' ').squeeze(' ').strip
    raise 'label empty' if label.empty?
    safe = label.gsub(/[^a-zA-Z0-9._-]+/, '-')[0, 48]
    safe = 'renamed' if safe.empty?

    stamp = if backup_id =~ /\A(\d{8}-\d{6})_/
      Regexp.last_match(1)
    else
      Time.now.strftime('%Y%m%d-%H%M%S')
    end
    new_id = "#{stamp}_#{safe}"
    new_dir = backup_dir(new_id, key)
    n = 2
    while File.exist?(new_dir) && new_id != backup_id
      new_id = "#{stamp}_#{safe}-#{n}"
      new_dir = backup_dir(new_id, key)
      n += 1
    end

    FileUtils.mv(old_dir, new_dir) unless old_dir == new_dir
    man_path = File.join(new_dir, 'manifest.json')
    if File.file?(man_path)
      m = read_json_file(man_path)
      m['label'] = label
      m['reason'] = label
      write_json_file(man_path, m)
    end
    self.bak_selected = new_id if bak_selected.to_s == backup_id
    new_id
  end

  def self.read_starter(key = nil)
    path = starter_pointer_path(key)
    return nil unless File.file?(path)
    read_json_file(path)
  rescue StandardError
    nil
  end

  def self.set_starter!(backup_id, key = nil)
    key = normalize_char_key(key || char_key || detect_char_key)
    src = backup_import_path(backup_id, key)
    raise "backup not found: #{backup_id}" unless File.file?(src)
    backs = list_backups(key)
    info = backs.find { |b| b['id'] == backup_id } || { 'id' => backup_id, 'label' => backup_id }
    dest_dir = File.join(starter_root, char_slug(key))
    FileUtils.mkdir_p(dest_dir)
    dest_import = File.join(dest_dir, 'import.json')
    FileUtils.cp(src, dest_import)
    pointer = {
      'kind' => 'saga-hl-starter',
      'version' => 1,
      'character' => key,
      'backupId' => backup_id,
      'label' => (info['label'].to_s.empty? ? backup_id : info['label']),
      'setAt' => Time.now.utc.iso8601,
      'importPath' => dest_import
    }
    write_json_file(starter_pointer_path(key), pointer)
    pointer
  end

  def self.load_starter_into_working!(key = nil)
    key = normalize_char_key(key || char_key || detect_char_key)
    ptr = read_starter(key)
    raise 'no starter set for this character' unless ptr
    path = ptr['importPath'].to_s
    path = starter_import_path(key) if path.empty? || !File.file?(path)
    raise 'starter import.json missing' unless File.file?(path)
    set = load_set_from_import_json(path, key)
    set['character'] = key
    self.working = set
    self.diff_cache = nil
    self.dirty = true
    set
  end
end
# END saga_hl/backup

# BEGIN saga_hl/compare
module SagaHl
  def self.norm_pattern_key(pattern)
    pattern.to_s.downcase.strip
  end

  def self.compare_field_val(h, name)
    case name
    when 'regex', 'bold', 'italic', 'underline', 'notify', 'wholeWord', 'caseSensitive', 'enabled'
      truthy_flag(h, name)
    when 'sound'
      s = h['sound'].to_s.strip
      s.empty? ? nil : s
    else
      h[name]
    end
  end

  def self.summarize_hl(h, gname)
    {
      'pattern' => h['pattern'].to_s,
      'color' => h['color'].to_s,
      'group' => gname.to_s.empty? ? nil : gname,
      'highlightType' => h['highlightType'].to_s.empty? ? 'general' : h['highlightType'].to_s,
      'scope' => h['scope'].to_s,
      'regex' => truthy_flag(h, 'regex'),
      'enabled' => h.key?('enabled') ? truthy_flag(h, 'enabled') : true,
      'wholeWord' => truthy_flag(h, 'wholeWord'),
      'caseSensitive' => truthy_flag(h, 'caseSensitive'),
      'id' => h['id'].to_s
    }
  end

  # Compare existing (baseline) vs proposed (working). Match by casefold pattern.
  def self.compare_sets(existing, proposed)
    ex_by = {}
    (existing['highlights'] || []).each do |h|
      k = norm_pattern_key(h['pattern'])
      next if k.empty?
      ex_by[k] = h
    end
    pr_by = {}
    (proposed['highlights'] || []).each do |h|
      k = norm_pattern_key(h['pattern'])
      next if k.empty?
      pr_by[k] = h
    end

    ex_groups = (existing['groups'] || []).map { |g| g['name'].to_s }.reject(&:empty?).uniq
    pr_groups = (proposed['groups'] || []).map { |g| g['name'].to_s }.reject(&:empty?).uniq

    report = {
      'character' => (proposed['character'] || existing['character']).to_s,
      'existingCount' => (existing['highlights'] || []).size,
      'proposedCount' => (proposed['highlights'] || []).size,
      'added' => [],
      'removed' => [],
      'changed' => [],
      'unchanged' => 0,
      'groupsAdded' => (pr_groups - ex_groups).sort,
      'groupsRemoved' => (ex_groups - pr_groups).sort
    }

    all_keys = (ex_by.keys + pr_by.keys).uniq
    all_keys.sort_by! { |k| (ex_by[k] || pr_by[k])['pattern'].to_s.downcase }

    all_keys.each do |key|
      ex = ex_by[key]
      pr = pr_by[key]
      if ex && !pr
        report['removed'] << summarize_hl(ex, group_name(existing, ex['groupId']))
        next
      end
      if pr && !ex
        report['added'] << summarize_hl(pr, group_name(proposed, pr['groupId']))
        next
      end
      ex_g = group_name(existing, ex['groupId'])
      pr_g = group_name(proposed, pr['groupId'])
      changes = []
      COMPARE_FIELDS.each do |fname|
        before = compare_field_val(ex, fname)
        after = compare_field_val(pr, fname)
        next if before == after
        changes << { 'field' => fname, 'before' => before, 'after' => after }
      end
      if ex_g != pr_g
        changes << { 'field' => 'group', 'before' => (ex_g.empty? ? nil : ex_g), 'after' => (pr_g.empty? ? nil : pr_g) }
      end
      if ex['pattern'].to_s != pr['pattern'].to_s
        changes << { 'field' => 'pattern', 'before' => ex['pattern'], 'after' => pr['pattern'] }
      end
      if changes.empty?
        report['unchanged'] += 1
      else
        report['changed'] << {
          'pattern' => pr['pattern'].to_s,
          'beforeGroup' => (ex_g.empty? ? nil : ex_g),
          'afterGroup' => (pr_g.empty? ? nil : pr_g),
          'changes' => changes,
          'id' => pr['id'].to_s
        }
      end
    end
    report
  end

  def self.diff_summary_line(report, baseline_label: 'live')
    a = (report['added'] || []).size
    r = (report['removed'] || []).size
    c = (report['changed'] || []).size
    u = report['unchanged'].to_i
    "#{baseline_label} #{report['existingCount']} -> working #{report['proposedCount']} (+#{a} / -#{r} / ~#{c} / =#{u})"
  end

  def self.baseline_set
    ensure_ui_defaults!
    if diff_baseline.to_s == 'live' || diff_baseline.to_s.empty?
      load_set_from_prefs(char_key)
    else
      load_backup_set(diff_baseline, char_key)
    end
  end

  def self.refresh_diff!
    ensure_working!
    ensure_ui_defaults!
    existing = baseline_set
    proposed = working
    self.diff_cache = compare_sets(existing, proposed)
    diff_cache
  end

  def self.diff_items(report = nil)
    ensure_ui_defaults!
    report ||= (diff_cache || refresh_diff!)
    case diff_filter.to_s
    when 'added' then report['added'] || []
    when 'removed' then report['removed'] || []
    when 'changed' then report['changed'] || []
    else
      (report['added'] || []).map { |x| x.merge('_kind' => 'added') } +
        (report['removed'] || []).map { |x| x.merge('_kind' => 'removed') } +
        (report['changed'] || []).map { |x| x.merge('_kind' => 'changed') }
    end
  end
end
# END saga_hl/compare

# BEGIN saga_hl/improve_dedupe
module SagaHl
  def self.parse_hex_color(color)
    s = color.to_s.strip
    return nil unless s =~ /\A#?([0-9a-fA-F]{6})\z/
    hex = Regexp.last_match(1)
    [hex[0, 2].to_i(16), hex[2, 2].to_i(16), hex[4, 2].to_i(16)]
  end

  def self.color_distance(a, b)
    ca = parse_hex_color(a)
    cb = parse_hex_color(b)
    return nil unless ca && cb
    Math.sqrt(ca.zip(cb).sum { |x, y| (x - y)**2 })
  end

  def self.colors_close?(a, b, max_dist: COLOR_CLOSE_DIST)
    d = color_distance(a, b)
    return false if d.nil?
    d <= max_dist
  end

  def self.rank_highlights(items)
    items.sort_by { |h| [hl_richness(h), h['enabled'] ? 1 : 0] }.reverse
  end

  # Exact pattern duplicates, plus casefold-same patterns when colors are close.
  # Keeps richest / enabled rule. Does not delete far-color casefold pairs.
  def self.improve_dedupe(set)
    highlights = set['highlights'] || []
    removed_exact = 0
    removed_color = 0

    by_exact = Hash.new { |h, k| h[k] = [] }
    highlights.each { |h| by_exact[h['pattern'].to_s] << h }

    survivors = []
    by_exact.each_value do |items|
      if items.size == 1
        survivors << items[0]
        next
      end
      ranked = rank_highlights(items)
      survivors << ranked[0]
      removed_exact += items.size - 1
    end

    by_fold = Hash.new { |h, k| h[k] = [] }
    survivors.each { |h| by_fold[h['pattern'].to_s.downcase.strip] << h }

    final = []
    by_fold.each_value do |items|
      if items.size == 1
        final << items[0]
        next
      end
      ranked = rank_highlights(items)
      keeper = ranked[0]
      final << keeper
      ranked[1..].each do |dup|
        if colors_close?(keeper['color'], dup['color'])
          removed_color += 1
        else
          final << dup
        end
      end
    end

    keep_ids = {}
    final.each { |h| keep_ids[h['id']] = true }
    set['highlights'] = highlights.select { |h| keep_ids[h['id']] }
    {
      'removed' => removed_exact + removed_color,
      'removedExact' => removed_exact,
      'removedCloseColor' => removed_color
    }
  end
end
# END saga_hl/improve_dedupe

# BEGIN saga_hl/editor
module SagaHl
  def self.current_set
    ensure_working!
  end

  def self.filtered_highlights
    ensure_ui_defaults!
    set = current_set
    items = (set['highlights'] || []).dup
    filt = browse_filter.to_s.downcase
    unless filt.empty?
      items.select! { |h| h['pattern'].to_s.downcase.include?(filt) }
    end
    typ = browse_type.to_s.downcase
    unless typ.empty? || typ == 'all'
      items.select! do |h|
        t = h['highlightType'].to_s
        t = 'general' if t.empty?
        t.downcase == typ
      end
    end
    grp = browse_group.to_s
    unless grp.empty? || grp == 'all'
      if grp == NO_GROUP
        items.select! { |h| h['groupId'].to_s.empty? }
      else
        items.select! { |h| h['groupId'].to_s == grp }
      end
    end
    case browse_sort.to_s.downcase
    when 'color'
      items.sort_by! { |h| [h['color'].to_s.downcase, h['pattern'].to_s.downcase] }
    when 'group'
      items.sort_by! { |h| [group_name(set, h['groupId']).downcase, h['pattern'].to_s.downcase] }
    when 'type'
      items.sort_by! { |h| [(h['highlightType'].to_s.empty? ? 'general' : h['highlightType'].to_s).downcase, h['pattern'].to_s.downcase] }
    else
      items.sort_by! { |h| h['pattern'].to_s.downcase }
    end
    items
  end

  def self.browse_page_slice
    items = filtered_highlights
    total = items.size
    pages = total.zero? ? 1 : ((total + BROWSE_PAGE_SIZE - 1) / BROWSE_PAGE_SIZE)
    self.browse_page = [[browse_page.to_i, 0].max, pages - 1].min
    start = browse_page * BROWSE_PAGE_SIZE
    slice = items[start, BROWSE_PAGE_SIZE] || []
    { 'items' => slice, 'total' => total, 'pages' => pages, 'start' => start, 'page' => browse_page }
  end

  def self.selected_highlight
    ensure_working!
    return nil if selected_id.to_s.empty?
    find_highlight(working, selected_id)
  end

  def self.select_rule!(token)
    ensure_working!
    token = token.to_s.strip
    # Prefer exact id match (ids may be numeric). Fall back to page index.
    h = find_highlight(working, token)
    if h
      self.selected_id = h['id']
    elsif token =~ /\A\d+\z/
      info = browse_page_slice
      idx = token.to_i
      h = info['items'][idx]
      raise "no rule at index #{idx} on this page" unless h
      self.selected_id = h['id']
    else
      raise "rule not found: #{token}"
    end
    selected_id
  end

  def self.set_rule_enabled!(id, on)
    ensure_working!
    h = find_highlight(working, id)
    raise "rule not found: #{id}" unless h
    h['enabled'] = !!on
    self.diff_cache = nil
    self.dirty = true
    h
  end

  def self.delete_rule!(id = nil)
    ensure_working!
    id = selected_id if id.to_s.empty?
    raise 'no rule selected' if id.to_s.empty?
    before = (working['highlights'] || []).size
    working['highlights'] = (working['highlights'] || []).reject { |h| h['id'].to_s == id.to_s }
    self.selected_id = nil if selected_id.to_s == id.to_s
    self.diff_cache = nil
    self.dirty = true
    before - (working['highlights'] || []).size
  end

  def self.delete_matching!
    ensure_working!
    ids = filtered_highlights.map { |h| h['id'].to_s }
    raise 'no matching rules' if ids.empty?
    working['highlights'] = (working['highlights'] || []).reject { |h| ids.include?(h['id'].to_s) }
    self.selected_id = nil if selected_id && ids.include?(selected_id.to_s)
    self.diff_cache = nil
    self.dirty = true
    ids.size
  end

  def self.bulk_enable_matching!(on)
    ensure_working!
    items = filtered_highlights
    raise 'no matching rules' if items.empty?
    items.each { |h| h['enabled'] = !!on }
    self.diff_cache = nil
    self.dirty = true
    items.size
  end

  def self.set_flag!(name, on, id = nil)
    ensure_working!
    name = name.to_s
    raise "unknown flag #{name}" unless FLAG_NAMES.include?(name)
    id = selected_id if id.to_s.empty?
    raise 'no rule selected' if id.to_s.empty?
    h = find_highlight(working, id)
    raise "rule not found: #{id}" unless h
    h[name] = !!on
    self.diff_cache = nil
    self.dirty = true
    h
  end

  def self.set_color!(hex, id = nil)
    ensure_working!
    s = hex.to_s.strip
    s = "##{s}" unless s.start_with?('#')
    raise "bad color #{hex.inspect}" unless s =~ /\A#[0-9a-fA-F]{6}\z/
    id = selected_id if id.to_s.empty?
    raise 'no rule selected' if id.to_s.empty?
    h = find_highlight(working, id)
    raise "rule not found: #{id}" unless h
    h['color'] = s.downcase
    self.diff_cache = nil
    self.dirty = true
    h
  end

  def self.set_pattern!(text, id = nil)
    ensure_working!
    text = text.to_s
    raise 'pattern empty' if text.strip.empty?
    id = selected_id if id.to_s.empty?
    raise 'no rule selected' if id.to_s.empty?
    h = find_highlight(working, id)
    raise "rule not found: #{id}" unless h
    h['pattern'] = text
    self.diff_cache = nil
    self.dirty = true
    h
  end

  def self.set_group!(name, id = nil)
    ensure_working!
    id = selected_id if id.to_s.empty?
    raise 'no rule selected' if id.to_s.empty?
    h = find_highlight(working, id)
    raise "rule not found: #{id}" unless h
    name = name.to_s
    if name.empty? || name == NO_GROUP || name.downcase == '(no group)'
      h['groupId'] = nil
    else
      g = find_group_by_name(working, name)
      unless g
        g = { 'id' => new_id('hlg1-'), 'name' => name, 'enabled' => true, 'collapsed' => false }
        working['groups'] << g
      end
      h['groupId'] = g['id']
    end
    self.diff_cache = nil
    self.dirty = true
    h
  end

  def self.discard_working!
    self.char_key ||= detect_char_key
    self.working = load_set_from_prefs(char_key)
    self.selected_id = nil
    self.diff_cache = nil
    self.dirty = true
    self.last_action = :discard
    working
  end

  def self.colors_for_dropdown(set = nil)
    set ||= current_set
    used = (set['highlights'] || []).map { |h| h['color'].to_s.downcase }.select { |c| c =~ /\A#[0-9a-f]{6}\z/ }
    (DEFAULT_COLORS + used).uniq
  end

  def self.truncate_text(text, max = 48)
    s = ascii_label(text)
    return s if s.length <= max
    "#{s[0, max - 3]}..."
  end
end
# END saga_hl/editor

# BEGIN saga_hl/pipeline
module SagaHl
  def self.ensure_toggles!
    self.toggles ||= {}
    IMPROVERS.each do |id, _label, default_on, _impl|
      toggles[id] = default_on unless toggles.key?(id)
    end
  end

  def self.improver_row(id)
    IMPROVERS.find { |i, _, _, _| i == id }
  end

  def self.implemented_improvers
    IMPROVERS.select { |_, _, _, impl| impl }
  end

  def self.toggle!(name)
    ensure_toggles!
    key = name.to_s.downcase.tr(' ', '_').to_sym
    key = :dedupe if key == :dedupe_exact
    row = improver_row(key)
    unless row
      raise "unknown improver #{name.inspect} - try: #{implemented_improvers.map { |i, _, _, _| i }.join(', ')}"
    end
    unless row[3]
      toggles[key] = false
      raise "#{key} is not implemented yet"
    end
    toggles[key] = !toggles[key]
    toggles[key]
  end

  def self.set_improver!(name, on)
    ensure_toggles!
    key = name.to_s.downcase.tr(' ', '_').to_sym
    key = :dedupe if key == :dedupe_exact
    row = improver_row(key)
    raise "unknown improver #{name.inspect}" unless row
    unless row[3]
      toggles[key] = false
      raise "#{key} is not implemented yet"
    end
    toggles[key] = !!on
    toggles[key]
  end

  def self.select_character!(raw_key)
    key = normalize_char_key(raw_key)
    self.char_key = key
    _n, inst = split_char_key(key)
    self.instance_filter = inst
    self.working = load_set_from_prefs(key)
    self.selected_id = nil
    self.diff_cache = nil
    if sync_source && normalize_char_key(sync_source) == key
      self.sync_source = nil
      self.sync_group_sel = nil
      self.sync_group_meta = nil
    end
    n = (working['highlights'] || []).size
    self.last_status = "selected #{pretty_char_label(key)} - #{n} rules"
    self.last_action = :char
    self.dirty = true
    key
  end

  def self.select_instance!(raw_inst)
    inst = raw_inst.to_s.strip.downcase
    raise "unknown instance #{raw_inst.inspect}" if inst.empty?
    self.instance_filter = inst
    keys = characters_by_instance[inst] || []
    if keys.empty?
      self.last_status = "no characters on #{pretty_instance(inst)}"
    elsif char_key && split_char_key(char_key)[1] == inst
      self.last_status = "instance #{pretty_instance(inst)} (CLI)"
    else
      want = char_name.downcase
      pick = keys.find { |k| split_char_key(k)[0] == want }
      pick ||= keys.max_by { |k| rule_count_for(k) }
      select_character!(pick) if pick
      self.last_status = "instance #{pretty_instance(inst)} (CLI)"
    end
    self.last_action = :instance
    self.dirty = true
    inst
  end

  def self.enable_standard_package!
    ensure_toggles!
    IMPROVERS.each { |id, _, _, _| toggles[id] = false }
    STANDARD_PACKAGE.each { |id| toggles[id] = true }
  end

  def self.run_improver(id, set)
    case id
    when :dedupe
      improve_dedupe(set)
    else
      { 'skipped' => true, 'reason' => 'not implemented' }
    end
  end

  def self.apply_pipeline(mode: :selected)
    ensure_toggles!
    enable_standard_package! if mode == :package

    # Prefer panel working set (e.g. post-Sync) so improvers/dedupe keep imports.
    before = working_for(char_key || detect_char_key)
    self.working = clone_set(before)
    bak = save_backup(before, reason: mode == :package ? 'before-package' : 'before-apply')

    results = {}
    IMPROVERS.each do |id, label, _, impl|
      next unless toggles[id]
      next unless impl
      results[id.to_s] = run_improver(id, working).merge('label' => label)
    end

    path = write_import(working)
    self.diff_cache = nil
    dedupe_note = ''
    if results['dedupe']
      rem = results['dedupe']['removed'].to_i
      exact = results['dedupe']['removedExact'].to_i
      close = results['dedupe']['removedCloseColor'].to_i
      dedupe_note = if rem.positive?
        " (deduped -#{rem}: exact -#{exact} close-color -#{close})"
      else
        ' (dedupe 0)'
      end
    end
    self.last_status = "Improve+write done - backup #{bak} - #{(working['highlights'] || []).size} rules#{dedupe_note}"
    self.dirty = true
    {
      'backup' => bak,
      'importPath' => path,
      'count' => (working['highlights'] || []).size,
      'beforeCount' => (before['highlights'] || []).size,
      'results' => results
    }
  end

  # Build selectable sync buckets: known groups + per-orphan-id + (no group).
  def self.build_sync_group_meta(source_set)
    groups = source_set['groups'] || []
    by_id = {}
    groups.each { |g| by_id[g['id'].to_s] = g }

    counts = Hash.new(0)
    samples = Hash.new { |h, k| h[k] = [] }
    types = Hash.new { |h, k| h[k] = Hash.new(0) }
    (source_set['highlights'] || []).each do |h|
      gid = h['groupId'].to_s
      key = if gid.empty?
        SYNC_NONE
      elsif by_id.key?(gid)
        gid
      else
        "#{SYNC_ORPHAN_PREFIX}#{gid}"
      end
      counts[key] += 1
      types[key][h['highlightType'].to_s.empty? ? 'general' : h['highlightType'].to_s] += 1
      samples[key] << h['pattern'].to_s if samples[key].size < 2
    end

    meta = []
    groups.each do |g|
      id = g['id'].to_s
      next if counts[id].to_i <= 0
      meta << {
        'id' => id,
        'label' => ascii_label(g['name'].to_s),
        'count' => counts[id],
        'kind' => 'group'
      }
    end

    counts.keys.select { |k| k.start_with?(SYNC_ORPHAN_PREFIX) }.sort_by { |k| -counts[k] }.each do |key|
      top_type = (types[key].max_by { |_, n| n } || ['general', 0])[0]
      sample = ascii_label(samples[key].first.to_s)[0, 28]
      sample = sample.empty? ? 'rules' : sample
      meta << {
        'id' => key,
        'label' => "other #{top_type}: #{sample}",
        'count' => counts[key],
        'kind' => 'orphan'
      }
    end

    if counts[SYNC_NONE].to_i > 0
      meta << {
        'id' => SYNC_NONE,
        'label' => '(no group)',
        'count' => counts[SYNC_NONE],
        'kind' => 'none'
      }
    end
    meta
  end

  def self.init_sync_groups!(source_key)
    src = load_set_from_prefs(source_key)
    self.sync_group_meta = build_sync_group_meta(src)
    self.sync_group_sel = {}
    (sync_group_meta || []).each { |m| sync_group_sel[m['id']] = true }
    sync_group_meta
  end

  def self.set_sync_group!(raw_id, on)
    token = raw_id.to_s
    self.sync_group_sel ||= {}
    if token == 'all'
      (sync_group_meta || []).each { |m| sync_group_sel[m['id']] = !!on }
      return sync_group_sel
    end
    id = if token =~ /\A\d+\z/
      m = (sync_group_meta || [])[token.to_i]
      raise "unknown sync group index #{token}" unless m
      m['id']
    else
      token
    end
    raise "unknown sync group #{id.inspect}" unless (sync_group_meta || []).any? { |m| m['id'] == id }
    sync_group_sel[id] = !!on
    sync_group_sel
  end

  def self.filter_set_by_sync_groups(source_set)
    selected = sync_group_sel || {}
    known = {}
    (source_set['groups'] || []).each { |g| known[g['id'].to_s] = true }

    keep_group_ids = {}
    highlights = (source_set['highlights'] || []).select do |h|
      gid = h['groupId'].to_s
      bucket = if gid.empty?
        SYNC_NONE
      elsif known[gid]
        gid
      else
        "#{SYNC_ORPHAN_PREFIX}#{gid}"
      end
      next false unless selected[bucket]
      keep_group_ids[gid] = true unless gid.empty?
      true
    end

    groups = []
    (source_set['groups'] || []).each do |g|
      groups << g.dup if selected[g['id'].to_s]
    end
    selected.each_key do |bucket|
      next unless bucket.start_with?(SYNC_ORPHAN_PREFIX) && selected[bucket]
      real_id = bucket.sub(/\A#{Regexp.escape(SYNC_ORPHAN_PREFIX)}/, '')
      next if groups.any? { |g| g['id'].to_s == real_id }
      label = (sync_group_meta || []).find { |m| m['id'] == bucket }
      name = label ? label['label'] : "Imported #{real_id[-8, 8]}"
      groups << {
        'id' => real_id,
        'name' => name,
        'enabled' => true,
        'collapsed' => false
      }
    end

    {
      'character' => source_set['character'],
      'highlights' => highlights.map(&:dup),
      'groups' => groups
    }
  end

  def self.sync_from!(source_raw)
    src_key = normalize_char_key(source_raw)
    tgt_key = normalize_char_key(char_key || detect_char_key)
    raise 'pick a different character to copy from' if src_key == tgt_key

    if sync_source.to_s.downcase != src_key || sync_group_meta.nil? || sync_group_sel.nil?
      self.sync_source = src_key
      init_sync_groups!(src_key)
    else
      self.sync_source = src_key
    end

    source_full = load_set_from_prefs(src_key)
    source = filter_set_by_sync_groups(source_full)
    selected_n = (sync_group_sel || {}).count { |_, v| v }
    total_g = (sync_group_meta || []).size
    raise 'select at least one group to copy' if (source['highlights'] || []).empty? && selected_n.zero?

    before = working_for(tgt_key)
    self.working = clone_set(before)
    bak = save_backup(before, reason: 'before-sync')
    report = merge_sets!(working, source, mode: 'skip', copy_groups: true)
    path = write_import(working)
    self.diff_cache = nil
    self.last_status = "synced from #{pretty_char_label(src_key)} (#{selected_n}/#{total_g} groups): +#{report['added']} skipped #{report['skipped']}"
    self.dirty = true
    {
      'backup' => bak,
      'importPath' => path,
      'count' => (working['highlights'] || []).size,
      'beforeCount' => (before['highlights'] || []).size,
      'report' => report,
      'source' => src_key
    }
  end
end
# END saga_hl/pipeline

# BEGIN saga_hl/messaging
module SagaHl
  # Story-window lines: always prefix [lich] so Saga filters catch our noise.
  # Do not use this for dialog XML (_respond).
  def self.story_echo(line)
    text = line.to_s
    text = text.sub(/\A\[lich\]\s*/i, '')
    echo "[lich] #{text}"
  end

  def self.import_restore_lines(info)
    path = info['importPath'] || last_import_path || import_path
    bak = info['backup'] || last_backup_id
    [
      '--- saga-hl: next steps ---',
      "1. Wrote #{path}",
      '2. Saga -> Import Settings -> Custom highlights -> that file',
      "3. Undo: pick a backup in Undo (or *hl restore #{bak})",
      '---------------------------'
    ]
  end

  def self.coach_line
    ensure_ui_defaults!
    set = working || empty_set(char_key || detect_char_key)
    n = (set['highlights'] || []).size
    case last_action
    when :apply, :package
      "Next: Saga -> Import Settings -> #{IMPORT_BASENAME} (improvers already ran)"
    when :write
      "Next: Saga -> Import Settings -> #{IMPORT_BASENAME} (no improvers ran)"
    when :sync
      'Synced into working set. Review Changes above, then Improve+write or Write only.'
    when :backup
      'Snapshot saved. Improve+write when you want a new import file.'
    when :restore
      'Backup copied to import file. Import Settings to load it.'
    when :discard
      'Working set reloaded from live prefs.'
    when :char, :instance
      n.zero? ? 'This character has no custom highlights yet.' : "Editing #{pretty_char_label(char_key)} - #{n} rules"
    else
      if last_backup_id.to_s.empty?
        'Tip: Backup first - safe snapshot before you change anything.'
      elsif n.zero?
        'Empty set - Sync from another character, or use saga-hl CLI for names.'
      else
        'Ready. Changes shows working vs live. Improve+write = improvers then file.'
      end
    end
  end

  def self.status_lines
    ensure_toggles!
    ensure_ui_defaults!
    self.char_key ||= detect_char_key
    set = working_for(char_key)
    lines = [
      "saga-hl  #{pretty_char_label(char_key)}  #{(set['highlights'] || []).size} rules",
      "  key: #{char_key}",
      "  import: #{last_import_path || import_path}",
      "  last backup: #{last_backup_id || '(none)'}"
    ]
    begin
      report = diff_cache || refresh_diff!
      lines << "  changes: #{diff_summary_line(report)}"
    rescue StandardError
      # ignore
    end
    implemented_improvers.each do |id, label, _, _|
      on = toggles[id] ? 'ON' : 'off'
      lines << "  [#{on}] #{label}"
    end
    lines << "  #{last_status}" if last_status.to_s != ''
    lines << "  coach: #{coach_line}"
    lines
  end
end
# END saga_hl/messaging

# BEGIN saga_hl/panel
module SagaHl
  def self.sanitize_xml(value)
    value.to_s.gsub('&', '&amp;').gsub('<', '&lt;').gsub('>', '&gt;').gsub("'", '&apos;').gsub('"', '&quot;')
  end

  # dropDownBox splits content_* on commas - never put commas in labels/values.
  def self.dropdown_safe(text)
    text.to_s.tr(',', ' ').gsub(/\s+/, ' ').strip
  end

  def self.open_dialog_xml
    "<closeDialog id='#{DIALOG_ID}'/><openDialog type='dynamic' id='#{DIALOG_ID}' title='saga-hl' target='#{DIALOG_ID}' scroll='manual' location='main' resident='false'><dialogData id='#{DIALOG_ID}'></dialogData></openDialog>"
  end

  def self.widget(tag, attrs)
    parts = attrs.map { |k, v| "#{k}='#{sanitize_xml(v)}'" }
    "<#{tag} #{parts.join(' ')} />"
  end

  def self.build_dialog
    ensure_toggles!
    ensure_ui_defaults!
    self.char_key ||= detect_char_key
    set = if working && working['character'].to_s.downcase == char_key.to_s.downcase
      working
    else
      begin
        load_set_from_prefs(char_key)
      rescue StandardError
        empty_set(char_key)
      end
    end
    rules = (set['highlights'] || []).size
    groups = (set['groups'] || []).size
    keys = list_character_keys

    out = String.new("<dialogData id='#{DIALOG_ID}' clear='t'>")
    y = 0
    w = PANEL_WIDTH

    # Header
    out << widget('label', id: 'hl_title', value: 'saga-hl', left: 2, top: y, width: 64, height: ROW_HEIGHT)
    out << widget('label', id: 'hl_char_name', value: pretty_char_label(char_key),
                  left: 70, top: y, width: 220, height: ROW_HEIGHT)
    out << widget('label', id: 'hl_stats', value: "#{rules} rules  #{groups} groups",
                  left: 300, top: y, width: 160, height: ROW_HEIGHT)
    out << widget('closeButton', id: 'hl_close', value: 'Close', cmd: '*hl close',
                  left: w - 86, top: y, width: 84, height: BTN_HEIGHT)
    y += BTN_HEIGHT + 4

    # Improvers
    out << widget('label', id: 'hl_imp_hdr', value: 'Improve', left: 2, top: y, width: w, height: ROW_HEIGHT)
    y += ROW_HEIGHT
    implemented_improvers.each do |id, label, _, _|
      checked = toggles[id] ? '1' : '0'
      out << widget('checkBox',
                    id: "hl_imp_#{id}",
                    text: label,
                    checked: checked,
                    checked_value: '1',
                    unchecked_value: '0',
                    cmd: "*hl set #{id} %hl_imp_#{id}%",
                    left: 8, top: y, width: w - 10, height: ROW_HEIGHT)
      y += ROW_HEIGHT
    end
    soon = IMPROVERS.reject { |_, _, _, impl| impl }.map { |_, lab, _, _| lab }
    unless soon.empty?
      out << widget('label', id: 'hl_soon', value: "Soon: #{soon.join(', ')}",
                    left: 8, top: y, width: w - 10, height: ROW_HEIGHT)
      y += ROW_HEIGHT
    end
    y += 4

    # Actions
    out << widget('label', id: 'hl_act_hdr', value: 'Do', left: 2, top: y, width: w, height: ROW_HEIGHT)
    y += ROW_HEIGHT
    out << widget('label', id: 'hl_act_hint',
                  value: 'Improve+write runs ON improvers then writes import. Write only skips improvers.',
                  left: 2, top: y, width: w, height: ROW_HEIGHT)
    y += ROW_HEIGHT
    btn_w = 118
    out << widget('cmdButton', id: 'hl_apply', value: 'Improve+write', cmd: '*hl apply',
                  left: 2, top: y, width: btn_w, height: BTN_HEIGHT)
    out << widget('cmdButton', id: 'hl_backup', value: 'Backup', cmd: '*hl backup',
                  left: 2 + btn_w + 6, top: y, width: 90, height: BTN_HEIGHT)
    out << widget('cmdButton', id: 'hl_write', value: 'Write only', cmd: '*hl write',
                  left: 2 + btn_w + 6 + 90 + 6, top: y, width: 100, height: BTN_HEIGHT)
    y += BTN_HEIGHT + 6

    # Copy-from
    out << widget('label', id: 'hl_copy_hdr', value: 'Copy from another character', left: 2, top: y, width: w, height: ROW_HEIGHT)
    y += ROW_HEIGHT
    others = keys.reject { |k| k.downcase == char_key.to_s.downcase }
    if others.empty?
      out << widget('label', id: 'hl_nosync', value: 'No other characters to copy from.',
                    left: 8, top: y, width: w - 10, height: ROW_HEIGHT)
      y += ROW_HEIGHT
    else
      flabels = others.map { |k| dropdown_safe(pretty_char_label(k, with_count: true)) }
      fvalues = others.map { |k| dropdown_safe(k) }
      want = sync_source.to_s
      fi = others.index { |k| k.downcase == want.downcase }
      if fi.nil?
        selected_from = 'Pick a character...'
        flabels = [selected_from] + flabels
        fvalues = ['_'] + fvalues
        fi = 0
      end
      out << widget('label', id: 'hl_from_lbl', value: 'Copy from', left: 2, top: y + 2, width: 64, height: DROP_HEIGHT)
      out << widget('dropDownBox',
                    id: 'hl_from',
                    value: flabels[fi] || flabels[0],
                    content_text: flabels.join(','),
                    content_value: fvalues.join(','),
                    cmd: '*hl syncsrc %hl_from%',
                    left: 70, top: y, width: w - 180, height: DROP_HEIGHT)
      out << widget('cmdButton', id: 'hl_sync', value: 'Sync', cmd: '*hl sync %hl_from%',
                    left: w - 100, top: y, width: 98, height: BTN_HEIGHT)
      y += DROP_HEIGHT + 2
      out << widget('label', id: 'hl_sync_hint',
                    value: 'Check groups below, then Sync. Changes summary updates after Sync.',
                    left: 2, top: y, width: w, height: ROW_HEIGHT)
      y += ROW_HEIGHT

      if sync_source && sync_group_meta && !sync_group_meta.empty?
        out << widget('label', id: 'hl_grp_hdr', value: 'Groups to copy', left: 2, top: y, width: 120, height: ROW_HEIGHT)
        out << widget('link', id: 'hl_grp_all', value: 'All', cmd: '*hl syncgrp all 1',
                      left: 130, top: y, width: 36, height: ROW_HEIGHT)
        out << widget('link', id: 'hl_grp_none', value: 'None', cmd: '*hl syncgrp all 0',
                      left: 170, top: y, width: 40, height: ROW_HEIGHT)
        sel_n = sync_group_sel.count { |_, v| v } rescue 0
        out << widget('label', id: 'hl_grp_count', value: "#{sel_n}/#{sync_group_meta.size} selected",
                      left: 220, top: y, width: w - 222, height: ROW_HEIGHT)
        y += ROW_HEIGHT
        sync_group_meta.each_with_index do |m, idx|
          checked = (sync_group_sel || {})[m['id']] ? '1' : '0'
          wid = "hl_sg_#{idx}"
          text = dropdown_safe("#{m['label']} (#{m['count']})")
          out << widget('checkBox',
                        id: wid,
                        text: text,
                        checked: checked,
                        checked_value: '1',
                        unchecked_value: '0',
                        cmd: "*hl syncgrp #{idx} %#{wid}%",
                        left: 8, top: y, width: w - 10, height: ROW_HEIGHT)
          y += ROW_HEIGHT
        end
      end
    end
    y += 6

    # Changes summary (working vs live prefs)
    out << widget('label', id: 'hl_chg_hdr', value: 'Changes (working vs live prefs)', left: 2, top: y, width: w - 200, height: ROW_HEIGHT)
    out << widget('cmdButton', id: 'hl_diff_ref', value: 'Refresh', cmd: '*hl diff',
                  left: w - 190, top: y, width: 80, height: BTN_HEIGHT)
    out << widget('cmdButton', id: 'hl_discard', value: 'Discard', cmd: '*hl discard',
                  left: w - 100, top: y, width: 90, height: BTN_HEIGHT)
    y += BTN_HEIGHT + 2

    begin
      report = diff_cache || refresh_diff!
      out << widget('label', id: 'hl_diff_sum', value: diff_summary_line(report),
                    left: 2, top: y, width: w - 4, height: ROW_HEIGHT)
      y += ROW_HEIGHT
      if (report['groupsAdded'] || []).any?
        out << widget('label', id: 'hl_ga',
                      value: truncate_text("groups +: #{report['groupsAdded'].map { |g| ascii_label(g) }.join(', ')}", 90),
                      left: 2, top: y, width: w - 4, height: ROW_HEIGHT)
        y += ROW_HEIGHT
      end
      if (report['groupsRemoved'] || []).any?
        out << widget('label', id: 'hl_gr',
                      value: truncate_text("groups -: #{report['groupsRemoved'].map { |g| ascii_label(g) }.join(', ')}", 90),
                      left: 2, top: y, width: w - 4, height: ROW_HEIGHT)
        y += ROW_HEIGHT
      end

      shows = %w[all added removed changed]
      svi = shows.index(diff_filter.to_s) || 0
      out << widget('dropDownBox', id: 'hl_diffshow',
                    value: shows[svi],
                    content_text: shows.join(','),
                    content_value: shows.join(','),
                    cmd: '*hl diffshow %hl_diffshow%',
                    left: 2, top: y, width: 120, height: DROP_HEIGHT)
      items = diff_items(report)
      total = items.size
      pages = total.zero? ? 1 : ((total + DIFF_PAGE_SIZE - 1) / DIFF_PAGE_SIZE)
      self.diff_page = [[diff_page.to_i, 0].max, pages - 1].min
      start = diff_page * DIFF_PAGE_SIZE
      slice = items[start, DIFF_PAGE_SIZE] || []
      stop = total.zero? ? 0 : [start + slice.size, total].min
      out << widget('cmdButton', id: 'hl_dprev', value: 'Prev', cmd: '*hl page -1',
                    left: 130, top: y, width: 60, height: BTN_HEIGHT)
      out << widget('cmdButton', id: 'hl_dnext', value: 'Next', cmd: '*hl page +1',
                    left: 196, top: y, width: 60, height: BTN_HEIGHT)
      out << widget('label', id: 'hl_drange',
                    value: total.zero? ? 'no deltas' : "#{start + 1}-#{stop} of #{total}",
                    left: 266, top: y + 2, width: 160, height: ROW_HEIGHT)
      y += DROP_HEIGHT + 4

      if slice.empty?
        out << widget('label', id: 'hl_diff_none', value: 'No changes vs live prefs.',
                      left: 8, top: y, width: w - 10, height: ROW_HEIGHT)
        y += ROW_HEIGHT
      else
        slice.each_with_index do |item, idx|
          kind = item['_kind'].to_s
          if kind.empty?
            kind = if item['changes']
              'changed'
            elsif diff_filter.to_s == 'removed'
              'removed'
            else
              'added'
            end
          end
          if kind == 'changed' || item['changes']
            bits = (item['changes'] || []).first(3).map { |ch| "#{ch['field']}:#{ch['before']}->#{ch['after']}" }.join(' ')
            line = truncate_text("~ #{item['pattern']}  #{bits}", 92)
          else
            marker = kind == 'removed' ? '-' : '+'
            en = item['enabled'] == false ? 'off' : 'on'
            g = item['group'] || '-'
            line = truncate_text("#{marker} [#{ascii_label(g)}] #{en} #{item['color']}  #{item['pattern']}", 92)
          end
          out << widget('label', id: "hl_drow_#{idx}", value: line, left: 4, top: y, width: w - 8, height: ROW_HEIGHT)
          y += ROW_HEIGHT
        end
      end
    rescue StandardError => e
      out << widget('label', id: 'hl_diff_err', value: "Diff error: #{e.message}",
                    left: 2, top: y, width: w - 4, height: ROW_HEIGHT)
      y += ROW_HEIGHT
    end
    y += 6

    # Restore
    out << widget('label', id: 'hl_undo_hdr', value: 'Undo (restore backup to import file)', left: 2, top: y, width: w, height: ROW_HEIGHT)
    y += ROW_HEIGHT
    backups = begin
      list_backups(char_key).first(RESTORE_PICK_LIMIT)
    rescue StandardError
      []
    end
    if backups.empty?
      out << widget('label', id: 'hl_nobak', value: 'No backups yet for this character.',
                    left: 8, top: y, width: w - 10, height: ROW_HEIGHT)
      y += ROW_HEIGHT
    else
      blabels = backups.map do |b|
        id = b['id'].to_s
        short = id.sub(/\A(\d{4})(\d{2})(\d{2})-(\d{2})(\d{2})(\d{2})_/) { "#{Regexp.last_match(2)}-#{Regexp.last_match(3)} " }
        short = short.split('_').first(2).join(' ')
        lab = ascii_label(b['label'].to_s)
        n = b['highlightCount']
        dropdown_safe(n ? "#{short} #{lab} (#{n})" : short)
      end
      bvalues = backups.map { |b| dropdown_safe(b['id']) }
      out << widget('dropDownBox',
                    id: 'hl_restore',
                    value: blabels[0],
                    content_text: blabels.join(','),
                    content_value: bvalues.join(','),
                    cmd: '*hl restore %hl_restore%',
                    left: 2, top: y, width: w - 4, height: DROP_HEIGHT)
      y += DROP_HEIGHT
    end
    y += 6

    out << widget('label', id: 'hl_sep', value: '---', left: 2, top: y, width: w, height: ROW_HEIGHT)
    y += ROW_HEIGHT
    out << widget('label', id: 'hl_coach', value: coach_line, left: 2, top: y, width: w - 4, height: ROW_HEIGHT)
    y += ROW_HEIGHT
    note = last_status.to_s.empty? ? 'Ready.' : last_status.to_s
    out << widget('label', id: 'hl_note', value: note, left: 2, top: y, width: w - 4, height: ROW_HEIGHT)

    out << '</dialogData>'
    out
  end
end
# END saga_hl/panel

# BEGIN saga_hl/commands
module SagaHl
  # Pure work + message list. No echo/_respond here - boot loop does that.
  # Sets dirty when the panel should redraw. Sets quit to exit.
  def self.handle_command(raw)
    cmd = raw.to_s.strip.sub(/\A<c>/i, '')
    cmd = cmd.sub(/\A;?saga[_-]?hl\s+/i, '').sub(/\A\*hl\s+/i, '')
    cmd = 'help' if cmd.empty? || cmd =~ /\Ahelp\z/i
    msgs = []
    ensure_ui_defaults!

    case cmd
    when /\Ahelp\z/i
      msgs.concat([
        'saga-hl workspace:',
        '  Modes: Browse | Diff | Backups | Tools  (*hl mode <name>)',
        '  Close / *hl close stops the workspace',
        '  Working character = logged-in (label only)',
        '  Browse: filter/type/group/sort, Sel/Del, flags/color/pattern',
        '  Diff: working vs live prefs or a backup',
        '  Backups: restore/load/rename/starter',
        '  Tools: improvers, Improve+write / Write only / Backup / Sync',
        '  *hl status | *hl discard | *hl diff | *hl diffshow <all|added|removed|changed>',
        '  *hl filter <text> | *hl page N | *hl sel <id|idx> | *hl del | *hl delmatch',
        '  *hl enable <id> 0|1 | *hl flag <name> 0|1 | *hl color <hex>',
        '  *hl pattern <text> | *hl group <name>',
        '  *hl bak rename <id> <label> | *hl bak starter <id> | *hl bak load-starter',
        '  *hl bak load <id> | *hl bak select <id>',
        '  *hl apply | *hl package | *hl backup | *hl write',
        '  *hl syncsrc <key> | *hl syncgrp all|N 0|1 | *hl sync <from-key>',
        '  *hl restore <id> | *hl char / *hl instance (CLI only)',
        "  live improvers: #{implemented_improvers.map { |i, _, _, _| i }.join(', ')}"
      ])
    when /\Astatus\z/i
      msgs.concat(status_lines)
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Aclose\z/i
      self.quit = true
      self.last_status = 'closing workspace'
      msgs << 'saga-hl: closing workspace'
    when /\Amode\s+(\S+)\z/i
      m = Regexp.last_match(1).downcase
      unless MODES.include?(m)
        msgs << "saga-hl: unknown mode #{m.inspect} - browse|diff|backups|tools"
      else
        self.mode = m
        refresh_diff! if m == 'diff'
        self.last_status = "mode #{m}"
        msgs << "saga-hl: mode #{m}"
        self.dirty = true
      end
    when /\Afilter(?:\s+(.*))?\z/i
      self.browse_filter = Regexp.last_match(1).to_s
      self.browse_page = 0
      self.mode = 'browse'
      self.last_status = "filter #{browse_filter.empty? ? '(cleared)' : browse_filter.inspect}"
      msgs << "saga-hl: #{last_status}"
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Atype\s+(\S+)\z/i
      self.browse_type = Regexp.last_match(1).downcase
      self.browse_page = 0
      self.mode = 'browse'
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Agroupf\s+(\S+)\z/i
      self.browse_group = Regexp.last_match(1)
      self.browse_page = 0
      self.mode = 'browse'
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Asort\s+(\S+)\z/i
      self.browse_sort = Regexp.last_match(1).downcase
      self.browse_page = 0
      self.mode = 'browse'
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Apage\s+([+-]?\d+)\z/i
      delta = Regexp.last_match(1)
      n = delta.to_i
      case mode.to_s
      when 'diff'
        self.diff_page = if delta.start_with?('+') || delta.start_with?('-')
          diff_page.to_i + n
        else
          [n - 1, 0].max
        end
      when 'backups'
        self.bak_page = if delta.start_with?('+') || delta.start_with?('-')
          bak_page.to_i + n
        else
          [n - 1, 0].max
        end
      else
        self.browse_page = if delta.start_with?('+') || delta.start_with?('-')
          browse_page.to_i + n
        else
          [n - 1, 0].max
        end
      end
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Asel\s+(\S+)\z/i
      begin
        select_rule!(Regexp.last_match(1))
        self.mode = 'browse'
        self.last_status = "selected #{selected_id}"
        msgs << "saga-hl: #{last_status}"
      rescue StandardError => e
        msgs << "saga-hl sel failed: #{e.message}"
      end
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Adelmatch\z/i
      begin
        n = delete_matching!
        self.last_status = "deleted #{n} matching rule(s)"
        msgs << "saga-hl: #{last_status}"
      rescue StandardError => e
        msgs << "saga-hl delmatch failed: #{e.message}"
      end
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Adel(?:\s+(\S+))?\z/i
      begin
        id = Regexp.last_match(1)
        n = delete_rule!(id)
        self.last_status = "deleted #{n} rule(s)"
        msgs << "saga-hl: #{last_status}"
      rescue StandardError => e
        msgs << "saga-hl del failed: #{e.message}"
      end
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Aenablematch\s+(\S+)\z/i
      begin
        on = %w[1 true on yes].include?(Regexp.last_match(1).downcase)
        n = bulk_enable_matching!(on)
        self.last_status = "#{on ? 'enabled' : 'disabled'} #{n} matching"
        msgs << "saga-hl: #{last_status}"
      rescue StandardError => e
        msgs << "saga-hl enablematch failed: #{e.message}"
      end
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Aenable\s+(\S+)\s+(\S+)\z/i
      begin
        id = Regexp.last_match(1)
        on = %w[1 true on yes].include?(Regexp.last_match(2).downcase)
        set_rule_enabled!(id, on)
        self.last_status = "enable #{id} -> #{on ? 1 : 0}"
        msgs << "saga-hl: #{last_status}"
      rescue StandardError => e
        msgs << "saga-hl enable failed: #{e.message}"
      end
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Aflag\s+(\S+)\s+(\S+)\z/i
      begin
        name = Regexp.last_match(1)
        on = %w[1 true on yes].include?(Regexp.last_match(2).downcase)
        set_flag!(name, on)
        self.last_status = "flag #{name} -> #{on ? 1 : 0}"
        msgs << "saga-hl: #{last_status}"
      rescue StandardError => e
        msgs << "saga-hl flag failed: #{e.message}"
      end
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Acolor\s+(\S+)\z/i
      begin
        set_color!(Regexp.last_match(1))
        self.last_status = "color set"
        msgs << "saga-hl: #{last_status}"
      rescue StandardError => e
        msgs << "saga-hl color failed: #{e.message}"
      end
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Apattern(?:\s+(.*))?\z/i
      begin
        set_pattern!(Regexp.last_match(1).to_s)
        self.last_status = 'pattern set'
        msgs << "saga-hl: #{last_status}"
      rescue StandardError => e
        msgs << "saga-hl pattern failed: #{e.message}"
      end
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Agroup\s+(.+)\z/i
      begin
        set_group!(Regexp.last_match(1).to_s.strip)
        self.last_status = 'group set'
        msgs << "saga-hl: #{last_status}"
      rescue StandardError => e
        msgs << "saga-hl group failed: #{e.message}"
      end
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Adiffshow\s+(\S+)\z/i
      f = Regexp.last_match(1).downcase
      unless %w[all added removed changed].include?(f)
        msgs << 'saga-hl: diffshow all|added|removed|changed'
      else
        self.diff_filter = f
        self.diff_page = 0
        self.mode = 'diff'
        self.dirty = true
      end
    when /\Adiff(?:\s+live)?\z/i
      begin
        self.diff_baseline = 'live'
        self.mode = 'diff'
        report = refresh_diff!
        self.last_status = diff_summary_line(report)
        msgs << "saga-hl: #{last_status}"
      rescue StandardError => e
        msgs << "saga-hl diff failed: #{e.message}"
      end
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Adiff\s+backup\s+(\S+)\z/i
      begin
        bid = Regexp.last_match(1)
        if bid == '_' || bid.empty?
          msgs << 'saga-hl: pick a backup for baseline'
        else
          self.diff_baseline = bid
          self.bak_selected = bid
          self.mode = 'diff'
          report = refresh_diff!
          self.last_status = diff_summary_line(report, baseline_label: "bak:#{bid}")
          msgs << "saga-hl: #{last_status}"
        end
      rescue StandardError => e
        msgs << "saga-hl diff backup failed: #{e.message}"
      end
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Adiscard\z/i
      begin
        discard_working!
        self.last_status = "discarded - reloaded #{(working['highlights'] || []).size} rules from prefs"
        msgs << "saga-hl: #{last_status}"
      rescue StandardError => e
        msgs << "saga-hl discard failed: #{e.message}"
      end
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Abak\s+select\s+(\S+)\z/i
      self.bak_selected = Regexp.last_match(1)
      self.mode = 'backups'
      self.last_status = "backup selected #{bak_selected}"
      msgs << "saga-hl: #{last_status}"
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Abak\s+load-starter\z/i
      begin
        load_starter_into_working!
        self.last_status = "loaded starter into working (#{(working['highlights'] || []).size} rules)"
        msgs << "saga-hl: #{last_status}"
      rescue StandardError => e
        msgs << "saga-hl bak load-starter failed: #{e.message}"
      end
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Abak\s+load\s+(\S+)\z/i
      begin
        bid = Regexp.last_match(1)
        bid = bak_selected if bid == '%hl_bakid%' || bid.empty?
        raise 'select a backup first' if bid.to_s.empty?
        set = load_backup_set(bid, char_key)
        set['character'] = char_key
        self.working = set
        self.bak_selected = bid
        self.diff_cache = nil
        self.last_action = :bak_load
        self.last_status = "loaded backup #{bid} into working (#{(working['highlights'] || []).size} rules)"
        msgs << "saga-hl: #{last_status}"
        msgs << '  Tip: *hl mode diff to review vs live.'
      rescue StandardError => e
        msgs << "saga-hl bak load failed: #{e.message}"
      end
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Abak\s+rename\s+(\S+)\s+(.+)\z/i
      begin
        bid = Regexp.last_match(1)
        label = Regexp.last_match(2).to_s.strip
        bid = bak_selected if bid.empty? || bid == '%hl_bakid%'
        raise 'select a backup first' if bid.to_s.empty?
        raise 'label empty' if label.empty? || label == '%hl_bakren%'
        new_id = rename_backup!(bid, label)
        self.bak_rename = label
        self.last_status = "renamed backup -> #{new_id}"
        msgs << "saga-hl: #{last_status}"
      rescue StandardError => e
        msgs << "saga-hl bak rename failed: #{e.message}"
      end
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Abak\s+starter\s+(\S+)\z/i
      begin
        bid = Regexp.last_match(1)
        bid = bak_selected if bid.empty? || bid == '%hl_bakid%'
        raise 'select a backup first' if bid.to_s.empty?
        ptr = set_starter!(bid)
        self.last_status = "starter set to #{ptr['backupId']} (#{ptr['label']})"
        msgs << "saga-hl: #{last_status}"
      rescue StandardError => e
        msgs << "saga-hl bak starter failed: #{e.message}"
      end
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Achar\s+(\S+)\z/i
      begin
        select_character!(Regexp.last_match(1))
        msgs << "saga-hl: #{last_status}"
      rescue StandardError => e
        msgs << "saga-hl char failed: #{e.message}"
      end
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Ainstance\s+(\S+)\z/i
      begin
        select_instance!(Regexp.last_match(1))
        msgs << "saga-hl: #{last_status}"
      rescue StandardError => e
        msgs << "saga-hl instance failed: #{e.message}"
      end
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Aset\s+(\S+)\s+(\S+)\z/i
      begin
        name = Regexp.last_match(1)
        rawv = Regexp.last_match(2).downcase
        on = %w[1 true on yes].include?(rawv)
        set_improver!(name, on)
        msgs << "saga-hl: #{name} -> #{on ? 'ON' : 'off'}"
      rescue StandardError => e
        msgs << "saga-hl: #{e.message}"
      end
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Atoggle\s+(\S+)\z/i
      begin
        name = Regexp.last_match(1)
        on = toggle!(name)
        msgs << "saga-hl: #{name} -> #{on ? 'ON' : 'off'}"
      rescue StandardError => e
        msgs << "saga-hl: #{e.message}"
      end
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Aapply\z/i
      begin
        info = apply_pipeline(mode: :selected)
        self.last_action = :apply
        msgs << "saga-hl: #{last_status}"
        msgs.concat(import_restore_lines(info))
      rescue StandardError => e
        msgs << "saga-hl apply failed: #{e.message}"
      end
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Apackage\z/i
      begin
        info = apply_pipeline(mode: :package)
        self.last_action = :package
        msgs << "saga-hl: #{last_status}"
        msgs.concat(import_restore_lines(info))
      rescue StandardError => e
        msgs << "saga-hl package failed: #{e.message}"
      end
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Abackup\z/i
      begin
        set = working_for
        self.working = set
        bak = save_backup(set, reason: 'manual')
        self.last_action = :backup
        self.last_status = "backup #{bak} (#{(set['highlights'] || []).size} rules)"
        msgs << "saga-hl: #{last_status}"
      rescue StandardError => e
        msgs << "saga-hl backup failed: #{e.message}"
      end
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Awrite\z/i
      begin
        set = working_for
        self.working = set
        path = write_import(set)
        self.last_action = :write
        self.last_status = "Write only: #{File.basename(path)} (#{(set['highlights'] || []).size} rules, no improvers)"
        msgs << "saga-hl: #{last_status}"
        msgs.concat(import_restore_lines('importPath' => path, 'backup' => last_backup_id || '(backup first)'))
      rescue StandardError => e
        msgs << "saga-hl write failed: #{e.message}"
      end
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Asyncsrc\s+(\S+)\z/i
      begin
        raw = Regexp.last_match(1)
        if raw == '_' || raw.empty?
          msgs << 'saga-hl: pick a character in Copy from'
        else
          self.sync_source = normalize_char_key(raw)
          init_sync_groups!(sync_source)
          n = (sync_group_meta || []).size
          msgs << "saga-hl: copy-from #{pretty_char_label(sync_source)} - #{n} group buckets (all selected)"
          self.last_status = "copy-from #{pretty_char_label(sync_source)}"
          self.mode = 'tools'
        end
      rescue StandardError => e
        msgs << "saga-hl syncsrc failed: #{e.message}"
      end
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Asyncgrp\s+(\S+)\s+(\S+)\z/i
      begin
        token = Regexp.last_match(1)
        rawv = Regexp.last_match(2).downcase
        on = %w[1 true on yes].include?(rawv)
        raise 'pick Copy from first' if sync_source.to_s.empty? || sync_group_meta.nil?
        set_sync_group!(token, on)
        sel_n = sync_group_sel.count { |_, v| v }
        self.last_status = "groups #{sel_n}/#{sync_group_meta.size} selected"
        msgs << "saga-hl: #{last_status}"
      rescue StandardError => e
        msgs << "saga-hl syncgrp failed: #{e.message}"
      end
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Async(?:\s+(\S+))?\z/i
      begin
        src = Regexp.last_match(1)
        src = nil if src.to_s == '_'
        src = sync_source if src.to_s.strip.empty?
        raise 'pick Copy from, check groups, then Sync (or *hl sync <char|instance>)' if src.to_s.strip.empty?
        info = sync_from!(src)
        self.last_action = :sync
        msgs << "saga-hl: #{last_status}"
        msgs << '  Tip: Open Diff to review, or Improve+write to dedupe, then Import Settings.'
        msgs.concat(import_restore_lines(info))
      rescue StandardError => e
        msgs << "saga-hl sync failed: #{e.message}"
      end
      self.dirty = true
    when /\Arestore\s+(\S+)\z/i
      begin
        bid = Regexp.last_match(1)
        bid = bak_selected if bid == '%hl_bakid%' || bid.empty?
        raise 'select a backup first' if bid.to_s.empty?
        path = restore_backup_to_import(bid)
        self.bak_selected = bid
        self.last_action = :restore
        self.last_status = "restored #{bid}"
        msgs << "saga-hl: #{last_status} -> #{path}"
        msgs << 'Saga -> Import Settings -> Custom highlights -> that file.'
      rescue StandardError => e
        msgs << "saga-hl restore failed: #{e.message}"
      end
      self.dirty = true
    else
      msgs << "saga-hl: unknown #{cmd.inspect} - *hl help"
    end
    msgs
  end
end
# END saga_hl/commands

# --- boot ---
# UpstreamHook only queues. File I/O + echo/_respond run on this script's
# main loop (same pattern as exp_sagapanel's heavy *exp refresh / importlogs).
# If the hook raises, Lich removes it - so keep the hook trivial.
SagaHl.ensure_toggles!
SagaHl.ensure_ui_defaults!
SagaHl.dirty = false
SagaHl.pending_cmd = nil
SagaHl.last_action = nil
SagaHl.sync_source = nil
SagaHl.sync_group_sel = nil
SagaHl.sync_group_meta = nil
SagaHl.quit = false
SagaHl.mode = 'browse'
begin
  # Panel always targets the logged-in character.
  SagaHl.char_key = SagaHl.detect_char_key
  SagaHl.working = SagaHl.load_set_from_prefs(SagaHl.char_key)
  SagaHl.ensure_instance_filter!
  SagaHl.last_status = "loaded #{SagaHl.pretty_char_label(SagaHl.char_key)} - #{(SagaHl.working['highlights'] || []).size} rules"
rescue StandardError => e
  SagaHl.last_status = "load failed: #{e.message}"
  SagaHl.char_key = SagaHl.detect_char_key
  SagaHl.working = SagaHl.empty_set(SagaHl.char_key)
  SagaHl.ensure_instance_filter!
end

# Match like exp/alsohere/timers: no \A anchor. Saga/FE often prefixes <c>.
hl_upstream_hook_id = "#{Script.current.name}_upstream"
UpstreamHook.remove(hl_upstream_hook_id) rescue nil
UpstreamHook.add(hl_upstream_hook_id, proc do |command|
  c = command.to_s.strip.sub(/\A<c>/i, '')
  if c =~ /\*hl\b/i || c =~ /;?saga[_-]?hl\b/i
    SagaHl.pending_cmd = c
    nil
  else
    command
  end
end, persist: false)

_respond(SagaHl.open_dialog_xml)
pause 0.2
_respond(SagaHl.build_dialog)

before_dying do
  UpstreamHook.remove(hl_upstream_hook_id) rescue nil
  _respond("<closeDialog id='#{SagaHl::DIALOG_ID}'/>")
end

SagaHl.story_echo('saga-hl workspace open (Browse/Diff/Backups/Tools). Close or *hl close to exit. *hl help.')
SagaHl.status_lines.each { |l| SagaHl.story_echo(l) }

loop do
  break if SagaHl.quit
  if SagaHl.pending_cmd
    raw = SagaHl.pending_cmd
    SagaHl.pending_cmd = nil
    begin
      SagaHl.handle_command(raw).each { |line| SagaHl.story_echo(line) }
    rescue StandardError => e
      SagaHl.story_echo("saga-hl error: #{e.message}")
    end
  end
  break if SagaHl.quit
  if SagaHl.dirty
    SagaHl.dirty = false
    _respond(SagaHl.build_dialog) unless SagaHl.quit
  end
  pause 0.2
end

UpstreamHook.remove(hl_upstream_hook_id) rescue nil
_respond("<closeDialog id='#{SagaHl::DIALOG_ID}'/>")
SagaHl.story_echo('saga-hl workspace closed.')
